  greatest scientists in recent history  modern Flat Earth beliefs mostly stem  back to the work of an English writer  called Samuel robofen who believed he'd  scientifically proven the flatness of  our planet with his famous Bedford level  experiment I did a whole video on that  recently so I won't go into detail here  except to say that when it comes to the  sharpness of tools in sheds so to speak  robofen was a [ __ ] sledgehammer as  well as believing girth was flat he also  thought he'd invented a miracle drug  capable of curing any disease this  apparent Panacea led to the deaths of  several people Brave or possibly foolish  enough to ingest it including robuffin's  own son in a way you could argue this  cure kind of worked corpses are  impervious to disease after all but the  fact their loved one no longer had that  nasty case of herpes probably wasn't  much of a consolation to the devastated  relatives of the deceased modern Hollow  Earth beliefs are usually attributed to  an American chap called John cleeve Sims  Jr he was born in the late 18th century  Sims made it his live submission to  spread his hollow Earth message far and  wide and by the 1820s he'd become so  influential that he very nearly  convinced the U.S government to fund an  expedition to find the giant entrances  to the underworld he believed were  located at the poles  but Sims was by no means the first  person to claim the Earth was Hollow in  fact almost every civilization in  history has had at least some kind of  concept of a hidden world beneath our  feet from the Aztecs to the Inuits not  to mention the fact that something  similar crops up in almost every major  religion hell in Christianity Shoal in  Judaism patala in Hinduism johannam in  Islam and naraka in Buddhism to name  just a few what I'm trying to say is we  humans have actually been kind of  obsessed with all things Hollow Earth  for a very long time but about 350 years  ago something strange happened hollow  Earth theory 