 thick and inside it  are two smaller shells surrounding a  solid core kind of like solar system  scale Russian dolls he believed these  shells were surrounded by a breathable  atmosphere and were therefore most  likely inhabited he also thought that  the northern lights were caused by gas  escaping from inside the earth and  interacting with Earth's magnetic field  several other important scientific  thinkers made their own additions to the  hollow Earth Concept in the centuries  after Halley's death including Scottish  physicists Sir John Leslie and first  president of Boston University William  Fairfield Warren amongst others as the  theory gained traction it began cropping  up in popular fiction too Jules Vern's  Journey to the Center of the Earth is  the most famous example but there are  literally thousands of stories based on  the hollow Earth theme even legendary  Italian womanizer Casanova got involved  though that man had a one-track mind so  instead of aliens or superhumans he  populated Earth's core with a bunch of  Randy hermaphroditic Dwarfs if you're  interested in reading that one by the  way it's called Iko samiron thought I'd  save you the trouble of trying to find  it by Googling Randy hermaphroditic  dwarves not a good idea but what does  all of this mean for hollow Earth theory  clearly it's been an important part of  culture and religion across the world  throughout human history and some of the  greatest Geniuses in recent memory have  been vocal believers  is it about time we started taking  Hollow earthas a bit more seriously  yeah no definitely not  the likes of kircher and Halle were  indisputably brilliant men but they were  also people of their time and much of  the signs we take for granted today  simply didn't exist in the 17th century  the collective knowledge of the human  race is a bit like a giant wall every  generation builds on the work of all  those who came before and the scientists  mathematicians and philosophers who are  dedicated enough to bring original ideas  into the world each get to lay a little  knowledge brick of their own on top of  the rest the men and women who are  pushing the boundaries today likely  aren't any more intelligent than  previous generations they simply have  the benefit of beginning their Journeys  much higher up the wall  Pali believed the Earth was Hollow  because it solved a problem he'd come  across in another area of Interest  magnetism at the end of the 17th century  he set off on a year-long voyage of the  Atlantic Ocean to study and map the  Earth's magnetic field the voyage was a  huge success but Holly had expected  Earth's magnetic field to be constant  and unmoving  a year of taking thousands of compass  readings all over the Atlantic showed  him that wasn't the case hollow Earth  theory was his attempt to make sense of  experimental results he didn't  understand in other words it was a  hypothesis if Earth's magnetic field was  fluctuating Hallie reasoned that  something must be interfering with it  competing magnetic fields from large  objects inside the Earth  perhaps of course his hypothesis was  completely wrong but he arrived at it  through experimental observation and  logical reasoning in other words he was  just a scientist doing science  the fact is pretty much every brilliant  scientist that's ever lived has believed  some weird and wonderful things that  would sound ridiculous today Charles  Darwin had no idea how genetic  inheritance actually worked despite it  being a fundamental part of his theory  of evolution and physicists Lord Kelvin  was convinced he calculated the exact  age of the Earth when in actual fact he  was off by about 4.4 billion years no  doubt the leading scientists of the  current generation will be shown to have  made a few major blunders of their own  in the not too distant future and hollow  Earth theory was undeniably a blunder  these days there's plenty of evidence  that proves Beyond doubt that our planet  isn't Hollow the fact that we all stick  to it through gravity for one thing a  hollow Earth like the one Sims envisaged  would have less than one percent of the  mass of a solid its sphere meaning  gravity at the surface would be a  fraction of what we actually experience  not to mention the fact that a  planet-sized shell of rock 500 Miles  thick would simply collapse on the video  wait  the scientists have determined the  composition of the planet by measuring  things like Earth's gravity magnetic  field and the progress of seismic waves  as they travel through the ground deep  beneath our feet that's how we know the  planet is made up of three main layers  the crust the mantle and the core none  of which would make a comfortable home  for a giant or a Nazi there really is no  room for ambiguity here but there is one  small problem with all of these pieces  of evidence they're all a little bit  esoteric making them fairly easy to  dismiss by anyone uninterested in taking  the time to understand them ultimately  the only Surefire way to make a hollow  Earth or believe the center of our  planet is solid would be to dig a giant  hole and setting them down there of  course they wouldn't get all that far  before the intense heat would literally  boil them alive  but hey sometimes the truth hurts thanks  for watching
 

